SPURS job chains/guards: reuse the slots of chains that were shut down and joined

Tokyo Jungle allocates a new job chain object, with two job guards, for every
area it loads (func_001502B0), and tears the old one down with
ShutdownJobChain + JoinJobChain and frees it (func_0014FBCC). The HLE's chain
and guard registries never released a slot, so after 16 area loads (32 guard
slots, two per load) cellSpursJobGuardInitialize returned
CELL_SPURS_TASK_ERROR_AGAIN and the game went into its own error loop
(sys_timer_sleep(1) forever): the game hung ~30 min into a session, every
thread asleep except SPU job workers.

A chain that was shut down and has been joined is now marked reusable, and so
are its guards; their slots are handed out only when no free slot is left,
so nothing changes until the point where the title used to stop.

--- a/libs/spurs/cellSpurs.c
+++ b/libs/spurs/cellSpurs.c
@@ -2243,6 +2243,7 @@
     volatile long running;   /* 1 while a host thread walks this chain */
     volatile long alive;     /* 1 until that host thread has actually exited  */
     volatile long stop;      /* set by Shutdown: the walker must leave        */
+    volatile long joined;    /* shut down and joined: the slot may be reused  */
 } s_jobchains[MAX_JOBCHAINS];
 
 /* The stop flag of the chain this host thread walks (NULL off a walker thread).
@@ -2259,6 +2260,7 @@
 
