+ * what keeps the registry from filling: Tokyo Jungle allocates a fresh chain
+ * object for every area it loads, and shuts down, joins and frees the old one,
+ * so the EAs never repeat. Without reuse the table was full after a few dozen
+ * area loads and the guards (below) ran out first: JobGuardInitialize
+ * returned AGAIN and the title stopped in its own error loop (sleep(1)
+ * forever, the screen frozen) about half an hour into a session. */
